#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:2
msgid "gpio-chardev interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"The `gpio-chardev` interface allows access to specific GPIO chardev lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:7
msgid ""
"Use  `snap interface gpio-chardev` to see which gpio chardev devices are "
"available on the system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:9
msgid ""
"$ snap interface gpio-chardev\n"
"name:          gpio-chardev\n"
"summary:       allows access to specific GPIO chardev lines\n"
"documentation: https://snapcraft.io/docs/gpio-chardev-interface\n"
"slots:\n"
"  - pi:bcm-gpio-0\n"
"  - pi:bcm-gpio-1\n"
"  - pi:bcm-gpio-10\n"
"[...]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:21
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:23
msgid "**Auto-connect**: no</br> **Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:23
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:25
msgid ""
"`source-chip` (slot, mandatory): list of alternative labels of the source "
"GPIO chip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:26
msgid "`lines` (slot, mandatory): GPIO lines present in the source chip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:28
msgid "Requires snapd 2.72+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:30
msgid ""
"Hardware IO interfaces covers some general considerations common to these "
"kinds of devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:32
msgid "When the interface is connected:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:33
msgid ""
"`snap-gpio-helper` sets up a virtual GPIO device exposing the specified "
"lines defined in the slot as a character device node at `/dev/snap/gpio-"
"chardev/<slot-snap>/<slot-name>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:34
msgid ""
"snapd sets up a symlink at `/dev/snap/gpio-chardev/<plug-snap>/<plug-name>` "
"pointing at the virtual slot device mentioned above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:36
msgid ""
"Once connected, the consuming snap can use the device via `/dev/snap/gpio-"
"chardev/<plug-snap>/<plug-name>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:38
msgid "Important considerations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:39
msgid "Slot definitions are only allowed for gadget snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:40
msgid ""
"This interface cannot be used if there is an active connection to the older "
"{ref}`gpio <interfaces-gpio-interface>` interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:41
msgid ""
"`source-chip` being a list enables sharing of a gadget snap between a number "
"of devices, for which the same lines are exposed by differently labeled GPIO "
"controllers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:42
msgid ""
"`lines` can be expressed by joining them with a comma: *n[,m]* or as a "
"range: *n-m* (inclusive) or a combination of both, assuming the ranges do "
"not overlap, e.g.: `lines: 0,2,4-8`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:43
msgid ""
"`lines` are exported in the order of presence in the source GPIO chip "
"device, and not in the order in which they are declared in the attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:44
msgid "Any given line can only be exported by one slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:45
msgid ""
"`gpio-aggregator` kernel module with configfs support is required (i.e. "
"UC24+)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:46
msgid "`gpio` interface will not work on UC26+ due to missing kernel support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:48
msgid "Migration from gpio to gpio-chardev"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:50
msgid ""
"Since `gpio` and `gpio-chardev` interfaces cannot be connected at the same "
"time, all existing `gpio` interface connections must be disconnected first "
"before connecting to `gpio-chardev`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:52
msgid ""
"This is only required if the gadget snap has both `gpio` and `gpio-chardev` "
"slots declared since performing a gadget refresh to a revision that only "
"declares `gpio-chardev` slots will automatically disconnect `gpio` "
"connections due to missing slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:54
msgid ""
"It is recommended to only have only one slot type on the gadget, either "
"`gpio` or `gpio-chardev`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-chardev-interface.md:56
msgid "Code examples"
msgstr ""

